          tips: {"image": "Choose, drop, or paste a local image. GIF input uses its first frame.", "effect": "Choose Pixelate, Blur, or Solid fill. Changes redraw all selected areas from the original image.", "strength": "Pixelate uses blocks from 4 to 64 pixels; Blur uses radius values from 2 to 40. Changes update the preview.", "color": "Solid fill replaces the selected pixels with this opaque color.", "entire": "Apply the effect to the whole image while keeping your drawn areas for later.", "format": "Download uses this format. Copy image always exports PNG. JPEG places transparent pixels on white.", "download": "Save a newly encoded image without dashed selection outlines or the original metadata.", "copy": "Copy a PNG without selection outlines. Use Download when this browser blocks image copying.", "undo": "Remove the most recently drawn area and redraw the remaining areas.", "clear": "Release the loaded image and cancel pending feedback while keeping the effect settings.", "selection": "Drag rectangles over the preview. Coordinates map to the original image; areas smaller than two pixels in either dimension are ignored."},
